$$
Using this information, we can calculate $u(x,T)$ as follows:
$$
0.1 \leq \int_{-\infty}^{+\infty} \psi_x(x-y,T) f(y) dy \leq 0.1 \int_{-\infty}^{+\infty} \psi_t(x-y,T) f(y) dy
$$
This gives us:
$$
0.1 \leq u(T) \leq 0.1 \int_{-\infty}^{+\infty} \psi_t(x-y,T) f(y) dy
$$
