$$
\psi_t(x-y,T)=e^{-(t/5)} [e^{-y/(t/5)}]^\prime
$$
To get rid of the factor $e^{-(t/5)}$, we can integrate by parts. To do this, let $v(y)$ be equal to $e^{-y/(t/5)}$ and let $w(x)$ be equal to $e^{-(t/5)}$. Then $v^\prime(y) = -e^{-y/(t/5)} / (t/5)$ and $w^\prime(x) = -e^{-(t/5)}/5$. So the integral becomes:
