$$
Now we need to calculate $v(w(x))$. This can be done using integration by parts again. For example, if $y$ goes from $-\infty$ to $+\infty$, then $v(w(x))$ becomes:
$$
v(w(x))=e^{-(t/5)} [w(x)]^\prime
$$
